Package: debos-toolbox
Version: 0.6.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-gi (>= 3.42), python3-gi-cairo, gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-glib-2.0, adwaita-icon-theme, librsvg2-common, pciutils, usbutils, curl, gpg, ca-certificates, bsdutils
Recommends: gir1.2-vte-3.91, pkexec | policykit-1, sudo, libnotify-bin, extrepo, flatpak, network-manager, xdg-utils, dconf-cli, xterm | x-terminal-emulator
Suggests: isenkram-cli, nvidia-detect, timeshift, inxi, fwupd, apt-listbugs
Maintainer: Hugo Moniz do Rego <hugomonizdorego@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/hugomonizdorego/Debos---Toolbox
Description: All-in-one GTK toolbox for Debian Stable, Testing, Sid and LMDE
 Debos - Toolbox keeps a Debian desktop healthy and personal from one window:
  - dashboard with health score and smart recommendations
  - cleaner (APT cache, unneeded packages, old kernels, logs, thumbnails,
    browser and Flatpak caches) with scan and clean
  - updates and switching between Debian Stable, Testing and Sid (deb822)
  - Repository Doctor: duplicate/conflicting entries, missing or expired GPG
    keys, legacy trusted.gpg, dead repositories; extrepo third-party repos
  - software center with Debian packages, vendor repositories and Flathub
  - desktop environments, window managers and login managers from Debian
  - kernels: Debian, backports, XanMod, Liquorix, Linux-libre and builds from
    kernel.org packaged as .deb; removal of kernels installed outside APT
  - hardware detection with driver and firmware recommendations
  - desktop tweaks, startup applications, default applications, templates
 .
 Administrative actions run as readable scripts in an embedded console with
 rights obtained through pkexec, sudo or su, and are logged to
 /var/log/debos-toolbox/tasks.log.
 .
 Developed in Timor-Leste. License: GNU GPL v3 or later.
